## 4. Downstream Behavioral Benchmark Tasks

To evaluate the functional impact of each lesion, we deploy a tripartite benchmark suite spanning generative fluency, affective semantics, and hierarchical syntactic parsing.

| Benchmark Task | Dataset & Protocol | Evaluated Metrics | Diagnostic Role |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **1. Predictive Fluency** | **WikiText-2** (Validation)<br>Sliding window ($W=512$, stride $S=256$) | • Perplexity: $\text{PPL} = \exp(\text{NLL})$<br>• Bits-per-character (BPC) | Global generative coherence & next-token prediction |
| **2. Semantic Valence** | **Stanford IMDB** (Test Split)<br>Zero-shot generative forced choice | • Binary Accuracy: $\mathbb{I}[\arg\max_{c} P(c) = y_{\text{gold}}]$<br>• Margin: $\Delta\text{LP} = \ln P(c_{\text{gold}}) - \ln P(c_{\text{distractor}})$ | High-level semantic sentiment representation |
| **3. Structural Parsing** | **Psycholinguistic Minimal Pairs**<br>Garden-path & SVA with attractors | • Garden-Path Ratio: $\frac{\text{Surprisal}(\text{Verb}_{\text{amb}})}{\text{Surprisal}(\text{Verb}_{\text{unamb}})}$<br>• Attractor Accuracy: $\mathbb{I}[P(v_{\text{agree}}) > P(v_{\text{mismatch}})]$ | Hierarchical syntax & long-range binding circuits |

---

### Task 1: General Fluency & Predictive Capacity (WikiText-2)
* **Dataset & Protocol:** Evaluated on the WikiText-2 validation set (200k+ tokens) using a sliding-window context of $W = 512$ tokens with stride $S = 256$:
  $$\text{NLL} = -\frac{1}{N} \sum_{i=1}^N \ln P(w_i \mid w_{<i}), \qquad \text{PPL} = \exp(\text{NLL}), \qquad \text{BPC} = \frac{\text{NLL}}{\ln(2) \cdot \text{Chars-Per-Token}}$$
* **Diagnostic Role:** Functions as an unconstrained global health check on output distribution coherence; sensitive to any perturbation degrading next-token language modeling.

---

### Task 2: Semantic Valence & Affective Discrimination (IMDB)
* **Dataset & Protocol:** Evaluated on Stanford IMDB polarized reviews using a zero-shot generative forced-choice format without task fine-tuning:
  $$\text{Prompt: } \text{"Review: } \{x\} \text{ \nQuestion: Is the overall sentiment positive or negative? \nAnswer: "}$$
* **Metrics:** 
  1. *Classification Accuracy:* $\text{Acc} = \mathbb{I}\!\left[\arg\max_{c \in \{\text{pos},\, \text{neg}\}} P(c \mid \text{prompt}) = y_{\text{gold}}\right]$
  2. *Log-Probability Margin:* $\Delta\text{LP} = \ln P(c_{\text{gold}} \mid \text{prompt}) - \ln P(c_{\text{distractor}} \mid \text{prompt})$
* **Diagnostic Role:** Probes whether high-level semantic sentiment survives circuit lesions, isolating diffuse lexical-thematic representations from surface generative fluency.

